From b1cf04d13584701ba4cb8cfd0835b0264215a650 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <alexander@auralite.local>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:02:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] X4 contract SDK: aura-sdk, aura-sdk-macros, reference
 contracts, ABI-JSON

A contract is written in Rust now:

* aura-sdk -- a no_std guest library: the seven ABI v1 functions as typed Rust,
  a length-exact fixed-layout codec, typed storage (Slot<T>, composed Key) and
  events with the published limits checked before the call. On the host the same
  source compiles against a mock backend that speaks the node's extern "C"
  contract, so the wrappers are tested rather than trusted.
* aura-sdk-macros -- #[entrypoint], #[constructor], #[migrate]: rename the
  annotated function and emit the extern "C" export the X3 lifecycle calls,
  rejecting a wrong arity or a non-u32 return at compile time.
* examples/{store,kv,events} -- three reference contracts, each its own
  workspace, built for wasm32-unknown-unknown (release + LTO + opt-level=z +
  panic=abort + strip + --max-memory=16MiB). Artifacts are committed and pinned
  by sha256; tools/build_contracts.py also writes examples/<name>/abi.json.
* docs/SDK.md -- how a contract is written, what it may contain and what it costs.

The gate found four real defects, all fixed here:

1. The X0 census rejected EVERY Rust contract: a mutable __stack_pointer, bulk
   memory (memcpy -> memory.copy) and call_indirect (core::fmt). The hosted
   policy now allows exactly one mutable global, only memory.copy/memory.fill,
   and call_indirect only when the element table contains no import -- so a
   function pointer can never reach host code. restrictive() is untouched, so
   every X0 verdict and NC stands.
2. rustc memory declares no maximum and X0 refuses unbounded memory: the
   canonical build passes -C link-arg=--max-memory=16MiB.
3. wasmi's Config was stricter than the census (mutable globals, bulk memory,
   reference types), so an accepted module was refused by the backend.
4. The codec could silently truncate a wider value read as a narrower type.

Gates: 253 tests, 4,624 vectors across 22 fixtures, 135 negative controls
(6 new), fmt/clippy clean, 239 external crates unchanged (syn/quote/proc-macro2
were already in the lock). Measured: store 5187 B / deploy 58495 / call 13115,
kv 5290 B / deploy 62353 / call 8506 / upgrade 62261, events 5033 B /
deploy 51330 / call 12940; artifacts byte-identical across two target dirs at
the same path.

Honest scope: hosted execution is still wasmi-only; a contract cannot allocate;
no serde; call_indirect is bounded but not verified (X8); no cross-contract calls
(X6); no caller checks (T-phase); reproducibility is path-scoped -- same
toolchain, flags and path only, and which contracts drift across paths was
measured to be unstable (one experiment: events only; a clean clone: store and
events).
